Backport of review fixes from CIX's pending mainline glue driver for the Sky1 USB3
controllers: "usb: cdns3: Add CIX Sky1 glue driver" (Hongliang Yang, v9, Nov 2026, not
merged yet; vendor file cdnsp-sky1.c), tested by CIX on the Orion O6.

- D3 entry: PME wake-up (PS_PME_En) is only armed when wake-up was requested (runtime
  suspend still arms it, a system suspend of a device not set up for wake-up no longer
  does). If the controller doesn't reach D3 after the retries, it is put back into D0
  with PME off instead of being left half way, and an error is returned (the vendor
  code printed an error and carried on as if it was suspended).
- System suspend: the AXI and SOF clocks are only gated once the controller's
  AXI_CLOCK_VALID has dropped. In device role, or when D3 entry failed, the controller
  is still running; gating its clocks then can hang the bus on the next access.
  Resume only re-enables what suspend gated, so the clock counts stay balanced.
- The D3 enter/exit and clock messages printed on every runtime suspend/resume of an
  idle controller (several lines every few seconds per port, with the kernel address
  of the xHCI registers) are now debug level.

